faq:
  title: Frequently Asked Questions
  list:
    - question: Can I try it before I pay?
      answer: >-
        Yes. Open the Extensions screen in an up-to-date copy of Manager, choose eInvoices.ae and
        create an account. The extension starts in the sandbox, where you can send your own sales
        invoices and credit notes as test e-invoices. They go from a test sender to a test receiver,
        so nothing reaches your customers or the Federal Tax Authority. Testing is free and needs no
        subscription.
    - question: How do I start sending real e-invoices?
      answer: >-
        Sign in at <a href="{app}">app.einvoices.ae</a> with the same account and subscribe for the
        number of legal entities that will send. Enrol each one by its TIN and register that TIN with
        A-Cube from the same page. Then finish onboarding in EmaraTax, by choosing “PLATFORM ACUBE
        TECHNOLOGIES L.L.C” in the list of e-invoicing service providers. Once the page shows the
        legal entity as active, switch the extension to Live in Manager and send.
    - question: Can I receive my suppliers' e-invoices?
      answer: >-
        Not yet. Today the extension sends sales invoices and credit notes. Receiving is not available
        yet.
    - question: What is Manager.io?
      answer: >-
        <a href="https://www.manager.io">Manager.io</a> is accounting software for small businesses.
        Its desktop and server editions are free. There is also a cloud edition, which is a flat fee
        for an unlimited number of businesses. The eInvoices.ae extension is
        <a href="#pricing">priced separately</a>.
    - question: What is the UAE eInvoicing mandate?
      answer: >-
        Businesses in the UAE have to exchange invoices as structured electronic documents instead of
        PDFs or paper. Each invoice is sent through an Accredited Service Provider over the Peppol
        network in the PINT AE format, and its tax data is reported to the Federal Tax Authority.
    - question: When do I have to start?
      answer: >-
        It depends on your revenue. Businesses with revenue of AED 50 million or more start on
        1 January 2027, and other businesses on 1 July 2027. See the <a href="#deadlines">deadlines</a>
        above.
    - question: Is eInvoices.ae an Accredited Service Provider?
      answer: >-
        No. eInvoices.ae is the extension that connects Manager to one. Your e-invoices are sent and
        received through <a href="https://www.acubeapi.com">A-Cube</a>, an Accredited Service Provider
        on the Peppol network. You appoint A-Cube as your service provider in EmaraTax; you do not need
        a separate contract with it.
    - question: Are there charges per invoice or credit note?
      answer: >-
        The monthly price covers {documents} invoices or credit notes, shared across all your legal
        entities. Each further one in that month is AED {extra}. Only those you send live are counted;
        test e-invoices sent in the sandbox are not. There are no other fees.
    - question: Is there an introductory discount?
      answer: >-
        Yes. Your first legal entity is AED {discount} per month cheaper for your first {months}
        months. After that it is AED {price} per month.
    - question: What counts as a legal entity?
      answer: >-
        Each company that issues invoices under its own name and Tax Registration Number. If you keep
        the books of three companies in Manager, that is three legal entities: AED {price} per month for the
        first and AED {additional} per month for each of the other two. The
        {documents} included invoices and credit notes are shared between them. A legal entity is identified by its TIN,
        and once enrolled it keeps its place on your subscription for 30 days before another can take it.
    - question: Do I need to change how I use Manager?
      answer: >-
        No. You keep creating invoices in Manager as you do now. To send one, open the extension in
        Manager and press Send beside it. The extension opens inside Manager; only your subscription
        is managed at <a href="{app}">app.einvoices.ae</a>.
    - question: How do I change or cancel my subscription?
      answer: >-
        Sign in at <a href="{app}">app.einvoices.ae</a>. There you can change the number of legal
        entities your subscription covers, and Manage billing opens the page where you update your
        card, see your invoices and cancel.
  help: How do I get help?
  helpAnswer: Email
cta:
